meta {
  name: Clone Radiology Tests
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/{{masterDataId}}/radiology-tests/clone
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "targetMasterDataId": "{{targetMasterDataId}}"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  masterDataId: 2db13b5e-4a25-412f-bcd9-68bcbeea9d59
  targetMasterDataId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:master_data__duplicate_test` — enforced by
  `PermissionGuard`; admins bypass, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` succeeds.

  Clone **all active** radiology tests from this master data (the `:masterDataId`
  in the URL, the *source*) into a target master data. Each flat test is copied
  with a fresh id, the target's `branchId`, and a fresh `versionHistory` v1.
  Returns `{ "copied": <n>, "skipped": <n> }`.

  A source test is **skipped** if its `testName` or `testCode` already exists
  (active) in the target. Both master data must belong to the caller's tenant
  (404 `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND` otherwise).

  Set `targetMasterDataId` to a second (usually different-branch) master data's
  id. The placeholder default will 404 until you set a real id.
}
